:"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"redhat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"cvss-base-score","object":"9","source":"cve","object_type":"number","object_canonical":"9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"cvss-severity","object":"CRITICAL","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"critical"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"date-published","object":"2026-07-20T14:18:18.318Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-07-20t14:18:18.318z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-07-22T18:13:49.559Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-07-22t18:13:49.559z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"description","object":"A path traversal vulnerability was found in pulpcore. The relative_path_validator function only verifies that content paths do not begin with \"/\" but fails to block directory traversal sequences such as \"../\" anywhere in the path. An authenticated administrator can craft a relative_path containing embedded traversal sequences (e.g., \"looking/normal/../../../../etc/shadow\") that escapes the intended export directory during FilesystemExport operations. Because the file content is also user-controlled (uploaded artifact), this allows arbitrary file write to any location writable by the Pulp service user, potentially leading to service compromise or further system exploitation.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a path traversal vulnerability was found in pulpcore. the relative_path_validator function only verifies that content paths do not begin with \"/\" but fails to block directory traversal sequences such as \"../\" anywhere in the path. an authenticated administrator can craft a relative_path containing embedded traversal sequences (e.g., \"looking/normal/../../../../etc/shadow\") that escapes the intended export directory during filesystemexport operations. because the file content is also user-controlled (uploaded artifact), this allows arbitrary file write to any location writable by the pulp service user, potentially leading to service compromise or further system exploitation."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.5 for RHEL 8","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.5 for rhel 8"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.5 for RHEL 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.5 for rhel 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.6 for RHEL 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.6 for rhel 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Satellite 6.16 for RHEL 8","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat satellite 6.16 for rhel 8"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Satellite 6.16 for RHEL 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat satellite 6.16 for rhel 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Satellite 6.17 for RHEL 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat satellite 6.17 for rhel 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Satellite 6.18 for RHEL 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat satellite 6.18 for rhel 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Satellite 6.19 for RHEL 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat satellite 6.19 for rhel 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.6","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.6"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.7","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.7"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Update Infrastructure 4 for Cloud Providers","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat update infrastructure 4 for cloud providers"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Update Infrastructure 5","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat update infrastructure 5"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-22","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-22"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"vendor","object":"Red Hat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12726","predicate":"assigner","object":"redhat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"redhat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12726","predicate":"cvss-base-score","object":"6.3","source":"cve","object_type":"number","object_canonical":"6.3"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12726","predicate":"cvss-severity","object":"MEDIUM","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"medium"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12726","predicate":"date-published","object":"2026-06-19T18:49:55.376Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-06-19t18:49:55.376z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12726","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-06-22T17:08:43.067Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-06-22t17:08:43.067z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12726","predicate":"description","object":"A flaw was found in the AWX GitHub webhook integration. When processing GitHub pull_request webhooks, the controller stores the pull_request.statuses_url value from the webhook payload without validating that it points to a trusted GitHub API endpoint. If a job template is configured with a GitHub Personal Access Token as its webhook credential, the controller later POSTs that token to the stored callback URL when posting job status updates. An attacker who can submit a correctly signed forged webhook using the job template's webhook_key can redirect the callback to an attacker-controlled URL and exfiltrate the configured GitHub PAT.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a flaw was found in the awx github webhook integration. when processing github pull_request webhooks, the controller stores the pull_request.statuses_url value from the webhook payload without validating that it points to a trusted github api endpoint. if a job template is configured with a github personal access token as its webhook credential, the controller later posts that token to the stored callback url when posting job status updates. an attacker who can submit a correctly signed forged webhook using the job template's webhook_key can redirect the callback to an attacker-controlled url and exfiltrate the configured github pat."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12726","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12726","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12726","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-918","source":"cve","object_type":"id",